<title>USA: Nebraska fed cattle bid $103.00/dressed-private.</title>
<headline>Nebraska fed cattle bid $103.00/dressed-private.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-02-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Nebraska feedlot cattle near midday Monday were not trading, bid $102.00 to $103.00 per cwt on a dressed basis but passed by owners pricing cattle at $104.00 to $105.00, market sources said.</p>
<p>The bulk of last week's cattle sold at $103.50/dressed, the sources said.</p>
<p>On a live basis, bids at $62.00 were passed by owners pricing cattle at $64.00, they said.</p>
<p>This week's showlist was expected steady to smaller than last week, despite a carryover from owners who passed on packer bids last week, the sources said.</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk 312-408-8720))</p>
